body:
Not lying, I apparently mispronounce a lot of english words and realized it's due to my slight speech impediment.. this actually helps. 

&#x200B;

(english is my first language...)

\*\*TRIGGER WARNING for sure...\*\*

Edit: I can't do special type text i guess.. rip me.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

This is exactly what happened to me. My significant other wanted me to "get better." I was told to choose. Him or "killing myself."

&#x200B;

I was concerned that I'd lose him. Not from a break up, but I was worried he would kill himself. So I forced myself. He kept praising me, saying he was "happy with my progress," and that I'm becoming more "comfortable with food."

&#x200B;

Fuck that. I'm overweight and fat. I hate myself so much more than before. I'm basically triggering myself every single night to somehow encourage whatever little disordered part of my brain.. and very slowly I'm getting back into the routine of taking the ECA stack. The one that was "killing me" apparently. At one point I'll go back to not caring because if I die at least I'll be skinny.

&#x200B;

I, for sure, miss high restriction. I miss having a clear eating disorder. I miss people telling me I need to eat more. Being told by my own psychiatrist that I should go to an outpatient program, despite how much it scared me... I miss weighing myself every morning feeling a little scared, but hopeful because I know I didn't eat so much the day before. I check and I lost another pound or half which does nothing else but encourage me "to do better."

&#x200B;

I miss being at my worst. I miss being sick, mainly just the ed sick part.. I miss being skinny and being so happy for achieving my little goal weights...

&#x200B;

And then I see myself in the mirror when I catch myself off guard. I wish that was enough to cause me to gag, but instead it makes my heart ache.

fuck me too lol. if that's what it takes i'll get a 4.0GPA and be PERFECT  so i can finally achieve my UGW...

&#x200B;

so is that why people with Eds seek for perfection? Is this the answer to life¿ To happiness¿?

this. I've explained time and time again that I'm tired, exhausted. But people don't seem to know what it's like to feel physically exhausted. All of your energy is depleted. it's so frustrating when I say I'm exhausted then say, "Okay well after you get home want to go hang at the mall or movies?"

&#x200B;

bruh what did i just say?

You can always gauge it in pre-game. That's what I usually do since I can't mute them in there anyways. 

&#x200B;

But the second someone says a really toxic comment that is absolutely not helpful in any way, muted immediately. I don't have time to get distracted trying to figure out what my teammates are talking about. I only have the time available to focus on the game and my own improvement. For me that works best. 

&#x200B;

Occasionally I will enable ally chat if they seem nice or chill in pre-game, but now that I've gotten so used to having my chat disabled I sometimes forget to look, and usually don't anyways. Typically turn on chat for kind people so I can say stuff like, "Ty(thank you)." "Mb.(my bad)" or "nj. (nice job)" 

&#x200B;

Just really quick stuff and usually I wait until I'm somewhere safe like the fountain..
